---
source: crates/skif-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: human.stdout
---
RULE                            CATEGORY   DEFAULT  FIXABLE    SUMMARY
empty-dependencies              manifest   error    safe       A dependency section (`dependencies`, `devDependencies`, `peerDependencies`, `optionalDependencies`) is an empty object.
root-package-private-field      manifest   error    safe       The root `package.json` must set `"private": true` so it cannot be published by accident.
root-package-manager-field      manifest   error    none       The root `package.json` must declare the package manager in `packageManager` or `devEngines.packageManager`.
root-package-dependencies       manifest   warning  unsafe     The root package should only have `devDependencies`; runtime dependencies belong to the packages that use them.
types-in-dependencies           manifest   error    unsafe     A private package lists `@types/*` packages in `dependencies`; type packages belong in `devDependencies`.
member-toolchain-fields         manifest   warning  unsafe     Member packages should not declare `packageManager` or `engines`; the root package owns the toolchain.
incompatible-peer-dependencies  manifest   warning  none       The version a package installs in `devDependencies` does not satisfy the range it declares in `peerDependencies`.
unsorted-dependencies           manifest   error    safe       The entries of a dependency section are not in alphabetical (byte) order.
unmatched-workspace-patterns    workspace  warning  unsafe     A workspace pattern does not match any directory.
missing-package-manifest        workspace  warning  unsafe     A directory matched by the workspace patterns has no `package.json`.
local-path-dependency           manifest   error    sometimes  A dependency points at a path on disk (`link:`, `file:`, `portal:` or a relative path) instead of a registry or workspace version.
version-mismatch                policy     error    sometimes  A dependency instance differs from the version its version group requires (highest, lowest, pinned, local or snapped).
banned-dependency               policy     error    unsafe     A dependency is declared although a banned version group forbids it.
semver-range-mismatch           policy     error    unsafe     A dependency uses a semver range other than the one its semver group requires.
policy-conflict                 policy     warning  sometimes  Two policies require incompatible outcomes for one dependency, or a group cannot be applied as configured.
invalid-local-version           policy     error    none       A workspace package has a `version` that is not an exact semver version, so dependents cannot align with it.
catalog-not-used                catalog    warning  sometimes  A dependency that has a catalog entry is declared with a version instead of `catalog:`.
catalog-mismatch                catalog    error    sometimes  A dependency is declared with a version while other packages take it from a catalog.
catalog-missing-entry           catalog    warning  sometimes  A dependency that should come from a catalog has no catalog entry.
unresolved-catalog-references   catalog    error    none       A `catalog:` specifier names a catalog or an entry that does not exist.
unused-catalog-entries          catalog    warning  none       A catalog entry that no manifest references.
workspace-protocol              policy     error    none       A dependency on a workspace package does not use the `workspace:` protocol.
unsynced-dependency-family      policy     error    none       Members of a dependency family declared in one package are on different versions.
